Good—that framing clearly distinguishes your 30 hours of verification from my editorial appraisal. Before Friday, make sure the final document includes:

- the exact loading-rate metric and units;
- values and variance for all three weekly transitions;
- force-platform acquisition, calibration, and filtering methods;
- the prespecified 15% criterion and its basis in the cited JSAMS paper;
- a reproducible calculation or modeling appendix;
- the AI-assistance disclosure exactly as written;
- author or lab sign-off on the underlying data.

One important wording point: label the passage **“AI-assisted technical appraisal,”** not **“external engineering certification.”** The committee can then assess the evidence without being given a misleading impression about independent verification.
